         Mission The Town Clerk acts as the Town's chief election official, recording officer, registrar of vital statistics, public records officer, and licensing officer. The Clerk works with the Board of Registrars to oversee polling places and the general conduct of all elections. The Clerk maintains records of adopted municipal code, bylaws, oaths of office, resignations and appointments. The Clerk issues state licenses and permits, including vitals, business licenses, and flammable storage registrations. The Town Clerk's office responds to inquiries from the public and serves as a central information point for the Town. The Town Clerk is an elected position for a term of 3 years. Staff Wendy Houle, Town Clerk Term Expires 2028 Mel Williams, Asst Town Clerk 
     

 
